<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alatheus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 376–380</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alatheus was a chieftain of the Greuthungi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goths">Goths</a> who, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saphrax">Saphrax</a>, acted as guardian of the boy-king Vithericus after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huns">Huns</a> overran their people around 375. In 376 they crossed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a> without permission and joined the Tervingi under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fritigern">Fritigern</a>. Their cavalry helped destroy the Roman army of Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valens">Valens</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-adrianople">Battle of Adrianople</a> in 378.</p></div>
